The regression recipe
A regression-based method treats each derivative as the outcome and the candidate terms as the predictors. The slides use three steps, and the figures add a fourth to check the result:

Compute the derivatives \(dX/dt\) from the data.
Propose a library \(\Theta(X)\) of candidate terms: here all 10 polynomials in \(x\), \(y\) and \(z\) up to degree 2.
Fit \(dX/dt \approx \Theta(X)\,\Xi\), where \(\Xi\) holds one weight per term and equation.
